cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPRUCE: training-free hierarchical exact-text context compilation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: McDaniel
    given-names: Myles
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rand0miz/spruce"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
keywords:
  - long-context
  - retrieval
  - language-models
  - context-compression
abstract: >-
  SPRUCE is a training-free hierarchical evidence compiler for long documents.
  It locates query-relevant source regions before the language model runs,
  expands them to paragraph boundaries, restores the exact original text in
  source order, and hands a frozen model a compact packet to read with
  ordinary dense attention. Measured numbers apply to the configuration,
  model, and hardware stated with each result.
